
Manufacturing — parts flowing through machines & workstations
Core classes

Part / Subassembly / Assembly / Product → MaintainableMaterialItem / MaterialComponent / Assembly

Machine / Workstation → PieceOfEquipment (located at a site)

Routing / Work instruction → PlanSpecification

Processing step → ManufacturingProcess ⊂ PlannedProcess

Part-at-Station state → MaterialState (the part being “at” a station during an interval)

Pattern

Part has participant at some time in ProcessingStep

ProcessingStep occurs in WorkstationSite (or located in at some time)

ProcessingStep hasInput Part (pre-state), hasSpecifiedOutput Part (post-state; same individual, new qualities)

PartAtStationState temporallyStartedBy check-in event; temporallyFinishedBy check-out event

ProcessingStep A precedes ProcessingStep B (routing order)

WorkInstruction prescribes ProcessingStep; ProcessingStep realizes WorkInstruction

Useful extras

Equipment capability: Machine hasFunction/hasCapability (e.g., weld, braze, coat)

Quality/measurement: MeasurementProcess on output; result is an InformationContentEntity linked via hasMeasuredValueAtSomeTime

Nonconformance: Event that isOutputOf a process; CorrectiveAction as a PlannedProcess that precedes rework step

Supply chain — Supplier ↔ Port ↔ Warehouse ↔ Plant
Core classes

Physical good / Lot / Container / Pallet → MaterialProduct / MaterialAggregate

Location nodes: Supplier site, Port, Warehouse, Plant → site (and/or Facility as a MaterialArtifact located in a site)

Shipment / Transport leg → MaterialLocationChangeProcess

Shipment order / BOL → Directive / DescriptiveInformationContentEntity

Item-in-Location state → MaterialState (good at a site during an interval)

Carrier / Supplier / Consignee → Organization with AgentRoles (SupplierRole, CarrierRole, CustomerRole)

Pattern

ShipmentLeg hasInput GoodOrContainer at OriginSite; hasOutput same GoodOrContainer at DestinationSite

ShipmentLeg occurs in SpatiotemporalRegion (captures transit)

ItemInLocationState for the good located in at some time Site with [from, to) derived from arrival/departure events

TransportPlan (route) prescribes the sequence of ShipmentLeg; legs meet or before/after each other via meets / precedes

BillOfLading / ASN describes ShipmentLeg and GoodOrContainer (quantities, identifiers)

Useful extras

Containerization: Good has continuant part at some time Container (or containedIn as a domain property)

Incoterms / handoff: Agreement prescribes risk transfer point; model as a process boundary where actsOnBehalfOfAtSomeTime switches from Supplier to Customer/Carrier

Delays & dwell: explicit Events between legs; keep ItemInLocationState for dwell analytics

Maintenance — Fault → Diagnostic test → Repair → Verification test
Core classes

Asset under maintenance: Engine / Assembly / Part

Fault / Symptom: Event or Disposition (quality) that inheres in the asset; often first recorded as an InformationContentEntity (fault report)

Diagnostic test: MeasurementProcess (e.g., borescope, ESAS measure, AEFR run)

Repair / Replacement / Adjustment: PlannedProcess (MaintenanceProcess)

Verification test: MeasurementProcess after repair

Work order: PlanSpecification; WorkCard/Task as sub-plans

Membership state (you already use): ComponentMembershipState for (Part↔Engine) with [start,end)

Pattern

FaultReport describes FaultEvent; FaultEvent isAbout Asset

DiagnosticTest recognizesAtSomeTime/measuresAtSomeTime the Fault on the Asset; may produce DiagnosticResult

RepairProcess has participant Asset (and possibly ReplacementPart as input/output)

For replacement: old Part isOutputOf removal; new Part isOutputOf installation; both processes temporallyStart/Finish corresponding ComponentMembershipStates

VerificationTest precedes return-to-service and recognizesAtSomeTime the absence or acceptable level of the original fault

WorkOrder prescribes DiagnosticTest, RepairProcess, VerificationTest; those processes realize the work order tasks

Causality & order: FaultEvent precedes DiagnosticTest precedes RepairProcess precedes VerificationTest


Component–Assembly (Partonomy & As-Built Configuration)
Core classes

Part / Subassembly / Assembly / Product → MaintainableMaterialItem / MaterialComponent / Assembly

PartKind / AssemblyType (e.g., TEC segment, flameholder segment, nozzle module) → Class-level types

As-built membership state (Part-in-Parent) → MaterialState

Installation / Removal → PlannedProcess / AssemblyProcess

Position / LCN / Slot → site (immaterial region on the parent)

Identifier → InformationContentEntity (PN, SN, LCN, ASN/ESN)

Pattern

Type-level partonomy (design/BOM):

PartKind componentPartOfAtAllTimes SubassemblyType

SubassemblyType componentPartOfAtAllTimes AssemblyType

AssemblyType componentPartOfAtAllTimes ProductType

Instance-level configuration (as-built):

Part(SN) componentPartOfAtSomeTime Parent(SN) (subassembly or assembly)

AsBuiltMembershipState has participant Part(SN), Parent(SN) and occupies temporal region [start, end)

AsBuiltMembershipState located in at some time LCN/Position site (if applicable)

Processes open/close membership:

Installation temporallyStarts AsBuiltMembershipState

Removal temporallyFinishes AsBuiltMembershipState

Installation/Removal has participant Part(SN), Parent(SN) (and Product/Engine if on-wing)

Transitivity & chain:

Membership is transitive via parent links; querying componentPartOf+ returns full chain (component → … → product)

Design vs as-built:

AssemblyType hasComponentPartAtAllTimes PartKind (design BOM)

Parent(SN) has continuant part at some time Part(SN) (as-built configuration)

Useful extras

Cascade logic: Removing an NHA temporallyFinishes all open child AsBuiltMembershipStates unless explicit evidence says otherwise.

Position fidelity: Bind LCN/Position to the membership state, not just the part—so you can answer “which SN was at position k at time T?”.

Effectivity & alternates: Model PartNumber supercededBy / alternateOf; attach effectivity (blocks, OFP, config) as qualifiers on design edges.

Single-parent constraint: A given Part(SN) has at most one active parent at a time; enforce no overlapping AsBuiltMembershipStates per parent.

Provenance & confidence: Put sourceTable, rowKey, confidence on the membership state (or the install/remove process) for auditability.

Condition overlay: Attach qualities (serviceable/unserviceable) and MeasurementInformationContentEntity (e.g., cycles since install) to the state interval.

Aggregation: Kits or rings (e.g., flameholder ring) can be modeled as object aggregates containing member parts; aggregates themselves may be componentPartOf higher assemblies.

Design–as-built alignment: Link each AsBuiltMembershipState isAbout the corresponding Type-level relation to keep BOM and configuration consistent.
